                <pb facs="0292" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg204"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Snyder to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-01-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 26,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Snyder reports that in Colombia’s official circles a rumor is current, as
                    coming from Reyes, that the Government of the United States has retreated from
                    its position and will permit the landing of Colombian troops at Panama, and
                    states that it is from this motive that Colombian forces are being organized. He
                    requests to be advised as to the situation.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
